  dispatch to a sink. It touches no environment globals — no [38;5;153mwindow[39m, no [38;5;153mprocess[39m, no direct [38;5;153mconsole[39m. Everything
  environment-specific arrives as an argument. That's what makes it testable in one place and what makes the transport
  seam real rather than aspirational.

  Its public surface is one factory:

  [33mcreateLogger[39m({ level, sink, clock }) [32m// → { debug, info, warn, error }[39m

  Each method takes [38;5;153m(event, fields)[39m — a short stable event name like [38;5;153m"login.attempt"[39m plus a flat object of data. Event
  names rather than free-form message strings, because the point of this is grepping production output, and
  [38;5;153m"login.attempt"[39m survives rewording in a way that [38;5;153m"Logging in: ..."[39m does not.

  The UMD footer is the whole of Approach A:

  [34mif[39m ([34mtypeof[39m module !== [31m"undefined"[39m && module.exports) {
    module.exports = { createLogger, resolveLevel, LEVELS };
  } [34melse[39m {
    window.AppLogger = { createLogger, resolveLevel, LEVELS };
  }

  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m gains [38;5;153m<script src="src/logger.js"></script>[39m immediately before the existing [38;5;153mapp.js[39m tag. [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m gains
  a [38;5;153mrequire('./logger')[39m. Neither [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m nor the existing module syntax changes at all.

  [1mThe transport seam, concretely:[0m [38;5;153msink[39m is a function [38;5;153m(record) => void[39m. Shipping logs remotely later means writing a
  second sink function and passing it in at the two wiring points — no call site in [38;5;153mapp.js[39m or [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m changes,
  because they only ever see [38;5;153mlogger.info(...)[39m. That's the property that made "console for now" a safe answer to the
  destination question.

  Wiring lives at each entry point rather than in separate adapter files: about four lines at the top of [38;5;153mapp.js[39m and
  three in [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m. With exactly two consumers, two more files would be ceremony — and the part actually worth
  testing (level resolution) is in the core, not the wiring.

  Does the structure look right before I go into the record shape and redaction?

